+### Multiple cursors
+
+`<Space>c` enables multi-cursor mode with a cursor at the current position
+(the word under it is remembered); press `<Space>c` again to add the next
+occurrence of that word, `<Space>C` to add every occurrence at once, and
+`Esc` to leave. While active:
+
+- Motions (`h j k l w b e`, `0 $ ^`, `G`, …) move **all** cursors together.
+- `i a I A` enter insert mode at every cursor; typing edits each one
+  (including `Enter`/`Backspace`/`Delete`).
+- `x` / `X` delete at every cursor; `p` pastes at every cursor.
+- The status bar shows the cursor count and every cursor is highlighted as a
+  block on screen.
+
+Each cursor's edit is a separate undo step, so undoing removes them one at a
+time.
+
 A leader followed by an unbound key just cancels the leader; `Esc` also
 cancels it.
 
